<rml>
<head>
    <title>Moments</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="scrim">
        <div class="case">

            <div class="lid stacked">
                <div class="lid-top">
                    <div class="head">
                        <div class="mark"></div>
                        <div class="title">Moments</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chrome">
                        <div class="win-btn" id="modal-close"><div class="glyph-x"><div class="bar a"></div><div class="bar b"></div></div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="hint">Up and down to choose, Enter takes you to the buttons, left and right between them, Escape or the pad's B goes back</div>
            </div>

            <!-- Nine slots: the autosave's, then eight of the player's. Built by the shell from the
                 slot files at the moment the screen opens (phase 77, .scaffold/states/): a thumbnail
                 where one exists, the name, the scene and the time. An empty slot says so and offers
                 itself. -->
            <div class="rows long" id="moment-rows"></div>

            <!-- Save here writes the focused slot (in play only; the launcher offers Resume alone),
                 Resume loads it, Delete removes it. Nothing here is one click from losing progress:
                 Delete asks twice, the same way Remove everything does. Two to a row (case.rcss,
                 .pairs), so none of the four is crushed in the panel. -->
            <div class="actions pairs">
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="moments-delete"><span class="act-label" id="moments-delete-label">Delete</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="moments-save"><span class="act-label" id="moments-save-label">Save here</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn act-play" id="moments-load"><span class="act-label" id="moments-load-label">Load</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn" id="moments-cancel"><span class="act-label">Cancel</span></div>
            </div>

            <!-- THE ONE LINE OF HONESTY, always shown (states-design.md section 8). -->
            <div class="foot">
                <span id="moments-note">A moment keeps your progress and where you stand. Enemies, platforms and effects start over, as when the game loads a file. Rewind is not offered: the program cannot freeze the game mid frame.</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
